{# ============================================================================
   Streaming Telemetry Deployment Template (platform-agnostic)
   ============================================================================
   New pipeline stage, closing the loop the earlier stages only open: they
   describe intent and push it to devices (the "write path"); this stage
   configures each device to push its own operational state back out (the
   "read path") -- design.md's Streaming Telemetry element, previously an
   unimplemented core element. Applied after logical topology.j2, before
   endpoint service.j2 (BAU) -- see scripts/render_configs.py's stage order.

   Render context expected (one device at a time, same convention as every
   other template here):
     site_telemetry : full parsed telemetry.yaml (site_telemetry)
     device_name     : hostname being rendered
     platform        : 'catalyst8000' | 'nexus93240' | 'catalyst9000'

   All resolution -- which sensor groups this device's role gets, and
   expanding each one from telemetry.yaml's catalog -- happens in
   device_telemetry_subscription() (filter_plugins/netascode_filters.py).
   This template only renders what that filter already resolved; no
   catalog lookups happen here, same "no lookups in the template itself"
   convention evpn_rr_peers()/endpoint_port_configs() established.

   NX-OS vs IOS-XE differ structurally here, not just by keyword (unlike
   physical/logical topology.j2's small per-line branches): NX-OS's
   `telemetry` feature is destination-group/sensor-group/subscription
   objects; IOS-XE's model-driven telemetry is a numbered `telemetry ietf
   subscription` block per sensor path. Both branches render from the same
   resolved site_telemetry data -- there is no separate per-platform model.

   FINDING -- not silently resolved, flagged instead: telemetry.yaml's
   sensor_paths are written as NX-OS DME paths (Cisco-NX-OS-device:...)
   only. The IOS-XE branch below reuses them as filter xpath values rather
   than substituting the equivalent Cisco-IOS-XE-*-oper YANG xpath, because
   no such mapping exists anywhere in this model yet -- confirm with the
   design owner whether telemetry.yaml should carry a per-platform path
   variant (mirroring how physical/logical topology.j2 branch on platform
   for small syntax differences) before deploying to a WAN or access
   device.

   A device whose role has no role_subscriptions entry in telemetry.yaml
   renders nothing but a NOTE -- a device simply not being covered yet is a
   documented gap, not a rendering failure.
   ============================================================================ #}
{% set subscription = site_telemetry | device_telemetry_subscription(device_name) %}
{% set dest = subscription.destination %}
!
{% if dest and subscription.sensor_groups %}
{% if platform == 'nexus93240' %}
feature telemetry
!
telemetry
  destination-group DG-{{ dest.name }}
    ip address {{ dest.ip_address }} port {{ dest.port }} protocol {{ dest.protocol | upper }} encoding {{ dest.encoding | upper }}
{% for sg in subscription.sensor_groups %}
  sensor-group SG-{{ sg.name }}
{% for path in sg.sensor_paths %}
    path {{ path }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% for sg in subscription.sensor_groups %}
  subscription {{ 100 + loop.index }}
    dst-grp DG-{{ dest.name }}
    snsr-grp SG-{{ sg.name }} sample-interval {{ sg.sample_interval_ms }}
{% endfor %}
! NOTE: sensor_paths above are taken directly from telemetry.yaml's NX-OS
! DME paths -- verify each against your exact NX-OS release's supported
! path list (e.g. "show telemetry transport all") before deploying.
{% else %}
{% for sg in subscription.sensor_groups %}
telemetry ietf subscription {{ 100 + loop.index }}
 encoding {{ dest.encoding | replace('-', '_') }}
{% for path in sg.sensor_paths %}
 filter xpath {{ path }}
{% endfor %}
 stream yang-push
 update-policy periodic {{ (sg.sample_interval_ms / 10) | int }}
 receiver ip address {{ dest.ip_address }} port {{ dest.port }} protocol {{ dest.protocol }}-tcp
!
{% endfor %}
! NOTE: update-policy periodic is in centiseconds (1/100s) on IOS-XE MDT,
! not milliseconds -- the value above is telemetry.yaml's
! sample_interval_ms divided by 10. filter xpath values are placeholders
! (see the FINDING above) -- this device's role needs the equivalent
! Cisco-IOS-XE-*-oper YANG xpath before this subscription will actually
! stream anything meaningful; not silently substituted here.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
! NOTE: no streaming telemetry subscription resolved for {{ device_name }}
! ({{ 'no destination' if not dest else 'no sensor groups' }} configured in
! models/telemetry.yaml's role_subscriptions for this device's role) --
! documented gap, not a render defect.
{% endif %}
!
end
